# Starhawk sound board -- netlist converted from MAME
#
# Cinematronics vector games carry a small audio board of their own, driven from the
# CPU board's output latch: the latch bits arrive here as ports (OUT_0 ... OUT_7, MAME's
# TTL_INPUT names), and the board's sound goes out to a final amplifier that MAME does
# not simulate and this file therefore does not contain.
#
# Source: MAME mame0289 (commit f34f02505e32), src/mame/cinematronics/nl_starhawk.cpp,
# NETLIST_START(starhawk). Licence CC0-1.0 by the file's own header (line 1),
# copyright-holders Aaron Giles (line 2).
# https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mamedev/mame/mame0289/src/mame/cinematronics/nl_starhawk.cpp
# Converted by tools/mame_netlist.py; checked by tools/build_board_nets.py.
#
# What the conversion means. MAME's netlists are written to be simulated, so this is a
# second reading of the sheet by someone else, not a read of it: designators and pin
# numbers are MAME's unless the notes say the sheet was read to correct them. Names on
# `label` lines are MAME's, which mostly follow the sheet's with Q for an overbar; `net`
# is used only for the supply rails. A `port` is a net that leaves what this file
# describes -- a signal from the CPU or the other board, a cabinet control, or a source
# MAME simulates with a stand-in rather than the circuit.
#
#   net NAME: PIN ...     a supply rail
#   label NAME: PIN ...   a net MAME names
#   wire PIN PIN ...      an unnamed connection
#   port NAME: PIN ...    a net that leaves this file (see above)
#   nc PIN ...            a pin with nothing attached
#   parallel PIN ...      outputs the board sums on one node by design
#   value REF VALUE       a passive's value, in the unit MAME's own macro uses
#
# PIN is DESIGNATOR.NUMBER. Diode pin 1 is the cathode; transistors keep B, C and E;
# MAME does not record which way round an electrolytic goes, so C pins are MAME's 1/2.
# The sheet numbers its ICs IC1, IC2 ...; they are written U1, U2 ... here, because the
# checker files every IC under a U designator.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Undone: what MAME does to simulate the board that the board does not do
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# line 27: #define HLE_SHIP_VCO 1 -> 0 (high-level stand-in for a real circuit)
# line 28: #define HLE_LAZER_VCOS 1 -> 0 (high-level stand-in for a real circuit)
# line 35: #define SLOW_SHIP_WOBBLE 0 -- kept as MAME has it (not a known kind of hack)
# line 436: dropped NET_C(R22.2, GND) -- the sheet takes R22 to 4C pin 2, the final amplifier's inverting input (R23 and the pot R25 as feedback), which MAME does not simulate; MAME grounds it instead
# line 601: NET_C(GND, IC5D.8, IC5D.9, IC5D.10, IC5D.12, IC5D.13, IC7C.3, IC7C.5, IC9E.3, IC9E.4, IC9E.5, IC9E.6) -> nc -- tied to GND in MAME's "Unconnected inputs" block
# line 463: RDUMMY is not a part -- a 100K to ground on the 556's output, which MAME's file says the board leaves unconnected
# Stand-ins that are not parts (the nets they drive are ports): TTL_INPUT(I_OUT_0), TTL_INPUT(I_OUT_1), TTL_INPUT(I_OUT_2), TTL_INPUT(I_OUT_3), TTL_INPUT(I_OUT_4), TTL_INPUT(I_OUT_7)
#
# Left out by MAME (commented out at TAG, so not in this file either):
#   line 88: RES(R20, 150)       -- part of final amp (not emulated)
#   line 89: RES(R21, RES_K(22)) -- part of final amp (not emulated)
#   line 91: RES(R23, RES_K(10)) -- part of final amp (not emulated)
#   line 92: RES(R24, 150)       -- part of final amp (not emulated)
#   line 93: POT(R25, RES_K(100))-- part of final amp (not emulated)
#   line 98: RES(R30, ???)
#   line 130: CAP(C1, CAP_U(2.2))
#   line 131: CAP(C2, CAP_U(2.2))
#   line 132: CAP(C3, CAP_U(3.3))
#   line 133: CAP(C4, CAP_U(3.3))
#   line 145: CAP(C16, CAP_P(470))    -- part of final amp (not emulated)
#   line 147: CAP(C18, CAP_P(470))    -- part of final amp (not emulated)
#   line 148: CAP(C19, CAP_P(470))    -- part of final amp (not emulated)
#   line 161: CAP(C39, CAP_U(1))
#   line 162: CAP(C40, CAP_U(1))
#   line 176: Q_2N6292(Q2)            // NPN -- part of final amp (not emulated)
#   line 177: Q_2N6107(Q3)            // PNP -- part of final amp (not emulated)
#   line 189: TTL_7815_DIP(IC2D)      // +15V Regulator -- not needed
#   line 190: TTL_7915_DIP(IC2C)      // -15V Regulator -- not needed
#   line 200: TL081_DIP(IC4C)         // Op. Amp. -- part of final amp (not emulated)
#
# This board's designators are column-and-row grid positions (IC5D, IC4A ...), written
# U5D, U4A here. MAME's file credits Jay Gallagher with verifying the PCB components.
#
# Compared with the sheet, Schematic, Audio Board (Star Hawk) 2-30008 Rev X3, 1-9-79 (doc
# 87193443ac92 p43; a 300 dpi 1-bit scan read from the native image at 2-6x; the manual has
# no parts list), 2026-10-20: every IC's type and position; the J2 inputs (J2-11 explosion,
# J2-12 and J2-13 lazers, J2-14 K on/off, J2-15 master on/off, J2-16 K exit -- MAME's OUT_0-4
# and OUT_7 in that order) with the 74LS04 6C and 7406 7C; the noise generator (6D, the
# 74LS164s 8C/8D/9C/9D, 9E, 10C/10D/10E, R1-R15, C7-C15, CR1, CR2, 6B and the CA3080 6A's
# inputs); the explosion one-shot and Q1 (R5, R7, R16, R17, C5, C6, C17); the killer-ship
# ramp, the 5D wobble oscillator and the ship VCO (R26-R38, CR3-CR6, C9, C20, C27, 4B, 5A,
# 5B); both lazer VCOs with their 74LS393 counters, 74S287 PROMs (the counter-to-PROM wiring
# read on 4E; 7E's tap numbers are illegible but wired the same) and DACs (R39-R60, C22-C26,
# CR7-CR10, Q4, Q5); and the TL182 3A with the summing node (6A pin 6, R19, C26, 3A pin 14,
# 3A pin 1 into 4A) all agree with MAME pin for pin and value for value, diode and transistor
# orientation included. 5D pin 5 is not drawn, so RDUMMY stands in for an open output. MAME
# differs only at the final amplifier: R22 goes into 4C pin 2, its inverting input, where
# MAME grounds it (line 436); corrected above.
#
# Open questions, as printed and not settled:
# * C21 (5D's timing capacitor, the ship-wobble rate) is printed "22 TANT 35V", 22uF. MAME
#   uses 0.22uF, marked "PCB verified", and keeps the sheet's 22uF behind its SLOW_SHIP_WOBBLE
#   debug switch (about 0.6 Hz against 60 Hz). This file follows MAME's board.
# * R6 (the explosion one-shot's timing resistor) is lettered "190K" against MAME's 150K;
#   190K is not a stock value and the print may be a slip. This file follows MAME.
#
# Labels that read wrongly on this scan but are MAME's designators by position: CR6 (reads
# like CR8), C26 (C28), R46 (R48). Not in this file: the final amplifier (4C, Q2, Q3, R20,
# R21, R23-R25, C16, C18, C19) and the regulators 2C and 2D, which are on the sheet with the
# values MAME's comments give.

# part U3A TL182
# part U4A TL081
# part U4B TL081
# part U4E 74LS393
# part U5A TL081
# part U5B TL081
# part U5D LM556
# part U5E 74S287
# part U6A CA3080
# part U6B TL081
